\title{PGViS: Personal Germline Variant Impact Score for Regulatory Regions}
\description{
An end-to-end, modular workflow for quantifying the burden of functionally disruptive germline variants in non-coding regulatory regions (splice donor/acceptor sites and transcription factor binding sites). PGViS goes from aligned reads (BAM) through joint germline variant calling, regulatory-region and dbSNP intersection, population allele-frequency resolution, reference/alternate sequence construction, DNABERT/DeepVRegulome model scoring, per-variant disruption metrics (log-odds ratio, score change, delta-Wi), and finally an ancestry-referenced per-sample composite score (PGViS). Heavy variant calling steps are shipped as parameterised shell templates; deep-learning scoring is delegated to the optional 'deepvregulome' Python package.
}
